Description: partition_alloc: serialize the initialization of the pools
 PartitionAddressSpace::Init() registers the pools in process-wide state, but
 it runs under PartitionRoot::lock_, a member of the root being initialized.
 Two roots initializing on two threads hold two different locks, both pass the
 IsInitialized() test, and the second one fails:
 .
   [FATAL:address_pool_manager.cc(62)] Check failed: !pool->IsInitialized().
 .
 Give the global initialization a lock of its own. A component build creates
 roots lazily per shared library, which turns a rare race into a build failure.
Author: Juan Manuel Méndez Rey <juan.mendezr@proton.me>
Forwarded: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8549218
Last-Update: 2026-10-28

